line	
line	<str>Use the blow kiss emote again</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ring in your inventory on her (you will not get it back)</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak with Prince Brand in the room directly south of the King. Continue to speak with him each time the dialogue box closes, until the dialogue is just "Good Day".</str>
line	
line	<str>After he recites the poem select "Be still, my heart"</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the Clap or Cheer emote in his room</str>
line	
line	<str>Keep speaking with him, agreeing with everything he says. Eventually the dialogue will just be "Good Day".</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the flowers on the prince</str>
line	
line	<str>Repeat the agreeing process</str>
line	
line	<str>Use (do not eat) the cake on him</str>
line	
line	<str>Repeat the agreeing process</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the dialogue goes "Hello, dear." and "Hello Darling." use the blow kiss emote in his room</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your ring on him and he will agree to marry you (silver and pineapple rings do not work)</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the castle and head east, across the bridge to the other castle. It's advised to clear the weeds from the herb and flax crops outside the main gates of the Miscellania castle every time you run past to save time on gaining favour which you need later on in the quest. If doing this, players can expect to have around 60% favour by the time they will need to gain the remaining favour.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak with Queen Sigrid upstairs</str>
line	
line	<str>Return west and speak with King Vargas</str>
line	
line	<str>Return east and speak with the Queen again</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back again and speak with Prince Brand in the room south of King Vargas to receive the Awful anthem</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak with Advisor Ghrim who is next to the King to turn the Awful anthem into a Good anthem</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the Good Anthem to the Queen to the East to get the Treaty</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the treaty back to King Vargas</str>
line	
line	<str>Leave the castle and head north to the anvil symbol</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak with Derrik with an iron bar in your inventory to receive a giant nib</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the giant nib on the logs in your inventory to create a Giant pen</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the King</str>
line	
line	<str>Buy Mixed flowers from Flower Girl. (This is the fastest but most click-intensive method, as each flower must be bought individually through dialogue. Exactly 1,875 GP is needed to go from the base 25% approval to the 75% minimum)</str>
line	
line	<str>Rake the herbs and flax outside the palace walls. (World hopping does NOT reset the patches, however weeds respawn in approximately 1 minute.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Mine coal on the north side of Miscellania.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Chop maple trees in the centre of Miscellania.</col>
